# Fixture: ASK redirection (migrating slot 12182: 7002 -> 7000)
# Key: foo (migrated 7002 -> 7000 via MIGRATE 127.0.0.1 7000 foo 0 5000)
# Exact RESP bytes:
#   source GET (no key locally): -ASK 12182 127.0.0.1:7000

#   target GET without ASKING: -MOVED 12182 127.0.0.1:7002
 (falls back to MOVED!)
#   ASKING -> +OK, then same-connection GET -> $3 bar

### 1. Setup (slot 12182 into migration)
$ redis-cli -p 7002 CLUSTER SETSLOT 12182 MIGRATING <id-7000>  -> OK
$ redis-cli -p 7000 CLUSTER SETSLOT 12182 IMPORTING <id-7002> -> OK
$ redis-cli -p 7002 MIGRATE 127.0.0.1 7000 foo 0 5000         -> OK

### 2. Source no longer has key -> ASK (NOT MOVED)
$ redis-cli -p 7002 GET foo
ASK 12182 127.0.0.1:7000


### 3. Target without ASKING -> MOVED back to owner (client must send ASKING first)
$ redis-cli -p 7000 GET foo
MOVED 12182 127.0.0.1:7002


### 4. Target with ASKING on SAME connection -> served
(raw TCP) ASKING -> +OK ; GET foo -> $3 bar   [verified 2026-09-25]

### 5. Key location oracles
$ redis-cli -p 7002 CLUSTER GETKEYSINSLOT 12182 10  -> (empty, key left)
$ redis-cli -p 7000 CLUSTER GETKEYSINSLOT 12182 10
foo

### 6. NODES migration markers
importing side (7000 view): [12182-<-<id-7002>] suffix on slot range
migrating side (7002 view): [12182->-<id-7000>] suffix on slot range
